    "result_text": "The full test suite is green. `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class and both of its tests pass.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe spec required `GET /api/owners/{id}` to return `contactPreference` = `\"EMAIL\"` when an email is present, otherwise `\"PHONE\"`. I implemented this following the existing pattern used for the other derived owner field (`membershipLevel`):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added a read-only `contactPreference` string property (enum `EMAIL`/`PHONE`) to the `Owner` schema, so the generated `OwnerDto` gains the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/org/springframework/samples/petclinic/model/Owner.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Transient` derived getter:\n   ```java\n   @Transient\n   public String getContactPreference() {\n       return (this.email != null && !this.email.isBlank()) ? \"EMAIL\" : \"PHONE\";\n   }\n   ```\n   MapStruct auto-maps it into `OwnerDto` by name (same mechanism as `membershipLevel`), so `RespondWithOwner` emits it with no wiring changes. The \"email present\" check mirrors the existing `getMembershipLevel()` logic (non-null and non-blank).\n\nBoth new acceptance tests (`corePhoneWhenNoEmail`, `functionalityEmailWhenPresent`) and the full suite pass: **Tests run: 2, Failures: 0, Errors: 0 \u2014 BUILD SUCCESS**.",
